 Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta                   6525 1451
 (SVN rev. 4867 )                                                 6525 1451
 by M.W.Herman et al [EMP,EMP-man].                               6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 6525 1451
  NDNUC= 150  NDEXCLUS= 20  NDEX= 201  NDLW= 100                  6525 1451
  LEVCC= 40  NDLV= 40  NDBR= 40  NDMSCS= 4                        6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                6525 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               6525 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
 This code integrates into a single system a number               6525 1451
 of important modules and features:                               6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 6525 1451
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      6525 1451
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  6525 1451
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                6525 1451
   and coworkers                                                  6525 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    6525 1451
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          6525 1451
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 6525 1451
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                6525 1451
   TRISTAN by H.Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                       6525 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      6525 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 6525 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                6525 1451
 - Hybrid Monte Carlo preequilibrium model(M.Blann)               6525 1451
   (code DDHMS by M.Chadwick, mod. by B.V.Carlson)                6525 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   6525 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                6525 1451
   discrete transitions                                           6525 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                6525 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                6525 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               6525 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 6525 1451
   library [RIPL]                                                 6525 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              6525 1451
   EXFOR library                                                  6525 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     6525 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 6525 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                6525 1451
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      6525 1451
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   6525 1451
 - Highly automated fitting of optical model                      6525 1451
   parameters (by B.V. Carlson)                                   6525 1451
 - KALMAN code for fitting experimental data and                  6525 1451
 - generating covariances                                         6525 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 6525 1451
 current evaluation:                                              6525 1451
                                                                  6525 1451
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-3+                      6525 1451
 library based on the 2015 version of ENSDF.                      6525 1451
 ENDF formatting enabled                                          6525 1451
 Exclusive emission from CN and target enabled                    6525 1451
 Exclusive spectra available for residues distant                 6525 1451
   from CN up to 3 neut. or 3 prot.                               6525 1451
 GSM level densities (Ignatyuk)                                   6525 1451
 GDR first hump width in 159Tb set to  3.48                       6525 1451
 GDR first hump energy in 159Tb set to 12.49                      6525 1451
 GDR first hump cross section in 159Tb set to  237.00             6525 1451
 GDR second hump width in 159Tb set to  4.00                      6525 1451
 GDR second hump energy in 159Tb set to 16.17                     6525 1451
 GDR second hump cross section in 159Tb set to  257.00            6525 1451
 Quasideuteron photoabsorption cross section normalized by a facto6525 1451
 CN decay and Direct cross sections added incoherently            6525 1451
 CN angular distribution assumed isotropic                        6525 1451
 Traditional Hauser-Feschbach Tlj_{CC}(E)=Tlj_{GS}(E-Egs)         6525 1451
 E1 strength function set to RIPL SMLO                            6525 1451
 GDR parameters from RIPL/MLO-exp.data+Plujko systematics         6525 1451
 Gamma-transition multipolarity set to    2                       6525 1451
